{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966780,"nonce":"l9EMzTNO7Q3AAkisZ8B9rSb0V0c=","title":"blinc_layout's crate-level allow(unused, dead_code) hides dead code; extracting any module","message":"`blinc_layout/src/lib.rs` line 1 is\n`#![allow(unused, dead_code, deprecated, mismatched_lifetime_syntaxes)]`.\nAcross ~58k lines that silences every unused import, unused local, and\nnever-called function in the crate.\n\n**Why:** a new crate carved out of blinc_layout does not inherit the\nattribute, so the first `cargo check` on it reports dead code that has\nbeen invisible for a long time. Extracting the CSS parser turned up nine\ndead items (`variable_name`, `CssBlock`, two `css_rule_with_errors*`\nvariants, `Stylesheet::resolve_variable`, `parse_transform` plus the two\nhelpers only it called, `parse_round_suffix`) and a `has_dot` flag that\nwas assigned but never read. It also exposed a doc comment that had\ndrifted onto the wrong function.\n\n**How to apply:** when extracting from blinc_layout, do not copy the\nblanket allow into the new crate. Budget a pass to verify each dead\nsymbol is genuinely unreferenced across the workspace, then delete it,\nand keep the new crate warning-free. Keep the workspace-wide\n`mismatched_lifetime_syntaxes` allow, which is a deliberate style choice.\n\nRelated: feedback sweep every crate you touch.","files":null}]}